Subject: [PATCH] kernel: Linux 4.4 compatibility for the legacy driver

* compat/linux-4.4: <linux/sched/*.h> and <linux/compiler_types.h> shims
  (split out of <linux/sched.h>/<linux/compiler.h> in 4.11/4.14) and a
  force-included header providing ALIGN_DOWN(), in_compat_syscall(),
  kvmalloc() and an empty __nocfi. Kbuild enables it only below 4.11.
* kernel_read()/kernel_write(): use the existing ksu_kernel_*_compat()
  wrappers. The pre-4.14 prototypes take (file, loff_t, char *, size) and
  the driver builds with -Wno-int-conversion, so direct calls compiled
  silently into pointer-as-offset reads on 4.4.
* full_name_hash(): two-argument form before 4.8.
* copy_to_iter(): 4.4 takes a non-const source buffer.

Verified: KernelSU-Next v3.4.0-legacy + this patch builds drivers/kernelsu
and links vmlinux on projects-nexus lavender 4.4.302 (AOSP clang r365631c).
---
diff --git a/kernel/Kbuild b/kernel/Kbuild
index 2d501753..d6e8246d 100644
--- a/kernel/Kbuild
+++ b/kernel/Kbuild
@@ -65,6 +65,14 @@ endif
 
 ccflags-y += -I$(KSU_KERNEL_DIR) -I$(KSU_KERNEL_DIR)/include
 
+# Linux < 4.11 (4.4/4.9 non-GKI): split sched headers, compiler_types.h and a
+# few helpers that the legacy driver expects. Never used on newer kernels.
+ifeq ($(shell test $(VERSION) -lt 4 -o \( $(VERSION) -eq 4 -a $(PATCHLEVEL) -lt 11 \) && echo y),y)
+$(info -- KernelSU-Next: Linux $(VERSION).$(PATCHLEVEL) compatibility layer enabled)
+ccflags-y += -I$(KSU_KERNEL_DIR)/compat/linux-4.4/include
+ccflags-y += -include $(KSU_KERNEL_DIR)/compat/linux-4.4/ksu_compat_44.h
+endif
+
 obj-$(CONFIG_KSU) += kernelsu.o
 
 LPATH := /usr/bin/env PATH="$$PATH":/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin
